# App version stamp

## Source of truth

- Version lives in [`package.json`](../../package.json) → `version` field.
- Bump `version` on every shippable change (patch/minor as appropriate).
- Build injects it via `vite.config.js` → [`src/config/version.ts`](../../src/config/version.ts).

## Visible in app

- Fixed stamp bottom-left on all routes (`AppVersionStamp` in `App.tsx`).
- Footer + admin header also show `vX.Y.Z`.

## Agent messages

**Every assistant reply must end with the current app version on its own line:**

```
— Trufi vX.Y.Z
```

Use the exact value from `package.json` at time of reply. If you bumped version in the same turn, use the new number.

Purpose: user compares chat footer vs on-screen stamp to confirm deploy / HMR applied.

## When bumping

- User-visible fix or feature → patch bump (e.g. 1.2.0 → 1.2.1).
- MVP slice or multiple files → minor bump if meaningful (e.g. 1.1.0 → 1.2.0).
- Always bump in the same commit/turn as the change you want verified.
